branchName.instructions:
Branch names must be:

- written in English;
- lowercase;
- in kebab-case;
- compact but meaningful;
- specific to the actual purpose of the branch;
- free of filler words, vague wording, and grammar mistakes;
- formatted as "<prefix>/<short-description>".

Use the most appropriate prefix:

- "feature/" — new user-facing or product functionality
- "fix/" — bug fixes
- "hotfix/" — urgent production fixes
- "refactor/" — internal code restructuring without behavior changes
- "chore/" — maintenance, cleanup, configuration, tooling, dependencies
- "docs/" — documentation changes
- "test/" — adding or improving tests
- "perf/" — performance improvements
- "ci/" — CI/CD, workflows, automation
- "build/" — build system, packaging, release tooling
- "style/" — formatting or code style only
- "experiment/" — temporary experimental work
- "spike/" — research or investigation without a guaranteed production result

Prefer short branch names with 2–6 words after the prefix.

Good examples:

- "feature/add-room-search"
- "feature/support-map-based-discovery"
- "fix/handle-empty-user-profile"
- "refactor/extract-auth-service"
- "chore/update-flutter-version"
- "docs/add-architecture-overview"
- "test/add-auth-flow-tests"
- "ci/add-release-workflow"

Avoid:

- overly long names;
- generic names like "feature/update", "fix/bug", "chore/changes";
- mixed casing;
- underscores;
- spaces;
- unnecessary articles like "a", "an", "the";
- unnecessary verbs like "make", "do", "change", unless they clarify the meaning.
